# Rank 1613 / CVE-2026-41242: protobuf.js accepted .proto message
# names without filtering, so a crafted type declaration containing
# __proto__ or other special characters reached the object model's
# keyed lookups and polluted Object.prototype for the parser's
# process (prototype pollution through an unfiltered type name,
# CWE-1321/CWE-75; #2124, fixed by #2127). The Type constructor in
# src/type.js stored `this.name = name` verbatim -- the name comes
# from the parsed .proto file. The fixing commit ff7b2afef8
# ("fix: filter invalid characters from the type
# name (#2127)", +1 line): `name = name.replace(/\W/g, "")` strips
# every non-word character before the name is stored. No pool
# correction.
#
# ATTENTION, identifier sanitisation at parse boundaries. The same
# untrusted-identifier family as ranks 1605 (Pritunl's profile id)
# and 1584 (Oro's query keys): the parser accepts an identifier from
# untrusted input and the object model uses it as a property key --
# nothing can ask "is every parsed identifier reduced to a safe
# alphabet before it becomes a property name", because the
# pollution happens through JavaScript's key semantics rather than
# an assignment rule can see. A binding on protobuf.js's own Type
# would detect this library rather than the weakness. Measured on
# the real code: scanning src/type.js reports zero findings at both
# revisions. No ENGINE-GAPS.md entry. No definition change shipped.
# Spec cve_rank1613 records the raw name store and the filtered
# form, both asserting reject VYQL-INJ-013: when parsed-identifier
# vocabulary lands, the raw form must flip to expect.

test "rank1613: the type name is stored verbatim"
  lang javascript
  file src/type.js
  reject VYQL-INJ-013
  code
  ```
  class Type extends NamespaceBase {

      constructor(name, options) {
          super(name, options);

          this.name = name;
          this.fields = {};
      }

      add(field) {
          this.fields[field.name] = field;
          return this;
      }
  }
  ```

test "rank1613: the fixed revision strips non-word characters"
  lang javascript
  file src/type.js
  reject VYQL-INJ-013
  code
  ```
  class Type extends NamespaceBase {

      constructor(name, options) {
          super(name, options);

          name = name.replace(/\W/g, "");
          this.name = name;
          this.fields = {};
      }

      add(field) {
          this.fields[field.name] = field;
          return this;
      }
  }
  ```
